{% comment %}
  Comments on a garden note, kept folded away until a reader asks for them.

  Nothing is requested from giscus.app — and no third-party frame is created —
  until the button is pressed, so a note that nobody comments on costs the
  reader nothing. The button is also why this exists instead of the theme's
  giscus.liquid, which loads the thread immediately.

  Renders nothing at all until giscus is actually configured (repo_id and
  category_id in _config.yml), rather than showing the theme's misconfiguration
  warning to visitors.
{% endcomment %}

{% if site.giscus.repo_id != blank and site.giscus.category_id != blank %}
  <div class="comments-toggle">
    <button class="btn btn-sm comments-toggle-btn" type="button" id="show-comments" aria-controls="giscus_thread" aria-expanded="false">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-comments"></i> show comments
    </button>
    <div id="giscus_thread" hidden></div>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('show-comments').addEventListener(
      'click',
      function () {
        const thread = document.getElementById('giscus_thread');
        thread.hidden = false;
        this.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        this.remove();
        const loader = document.createElement('script');
        loader.src = "{{ '/assets/js/giscus-setup.js' | relative_url }}";
        document.body.appendChild(loader);
      },
      { once: true }
    );
  </script>
{% endif %}
